Linux links distribution-provided libraries rather than vendoring their code:
- FFmpeg libavcodec, libavutil, libswscale, libswresample:
  https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
  Most FFmpeg code is LGPL-2.1-or-later; optional components change the effective
  build license to GPL. Check the chosen distribution's build/license notices.
  No FDK-AAC dependency is used.
- GTK 3 / GLib: LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://www.gtk.org/
- Ayatana AppIndicator: LGPL-2.1-or-later or LGPL-3.0,
  https://github.com/AyatanaIndicators/libayatana-appindicator
- PulseAudio: LGPL-2.1-or-later client libraries, https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/PulseAudio/
- Avahi: LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://avahi.org/
- OpenSSL: Apache-2.0 for OpenSSL 3, https://www.openssl.org/source/license.html
- libplist: LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://github.com/libimobiledevice/libplist

